                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>On December 8, at the Bermuda Conference, Jean-Marc Boegner of the French
                    Delegation transmitted to Douglas MacArthur II of the United States Delegation a
                    memorandum in which the French Government expressed interest in cooperation with
                    the United States, the United Kingdom, and Canada in the field of atomic energy,
                    particularly with regard to the exchange of information. For a memorandum of the
                    MacArthur–Boegner conversation of December 8, see <ref
                        target="frus:frus1952-54v05p2/pg_1845">volume <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >v</hi>, Part 2, page 1845</ref>. A translation of the French memorandum
                    is in file 600.0012/12–6853.</p>
            </div>
